--------------------- CableDyn Input File ------------------------------------
CableDyn input file: IEA-15MW VolturnUS-S (OpenFAST, CompMooring = 5), line 1 breaks at its fairlead at t = 100 s
-- CableDyn_UMaine.dat with a FAILURE row: at t = 100 s line 1 detaches from its fairlead and its
-- end falls freely, while OpenFAST carries on with the platform moored by lines 2 and 3. This is
-- the accidental-limit-state (ALS) case of a broken mooring line. FairTen1 drops to near zero at
-- the break; FairTen2/3 and AnchTen2/3 give the intact-line response and the ElastoDyn PtfmSurge/
-- PtfmSway channels the platform drift. A tension trigger (FailTen) breaks the line instead when
-- its fairlead tension first reaches a threshold.
